    {
      "id": 42,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        2200,
        540
      ],
      "size": [
        380,
        320
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 41,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "widgets_values": [
        "WHY THE CROP IS OUTSIDE\n\nThe carried frames have to line up pixel for pixel with what\nfollows them. A box computed per chunk would move between chunks,\nso the pin would fight the generation instead of anchoring it \u2014\nH3 Chunk Context refuses outright if it sees two sizes.\n\nOne box for the whole clip also means every chunk decodes at the\nsame size, so they join at crop size and uncrop ONCE at the end.\n\nThe cost: on a clip where she crosses the frame, that one box is\nthe union of everywhere she goes, and the subject gets fewer\npixels than a per-chunk box would give her."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 43,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        2200,
        880
      ],
      "size": [
        380,
        260
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 42,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "widgets_values": [
        "AUDIO\n\nH3MaskInpaint has keep_audio TRUE, so the audio latent is pinned\nto the source and a decode would hand back the source track,\nre-rendered. The source audio goes straight to the muxer instead.\n\nTurn keep_audio off and that stops being true: Close joins IMAGE\nonly, so model-generated audio would need its own join."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
